<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

     Privileged permission allowlist for DomaWifiRelay.

     WHY THIS FILE IS REQUIRED.
     READ_WIFI_CREDENTIAL is signature|privileged, not signature:

         frameworks/base/core/res/AndroidManifest.xml
           2402  <permission android:name="android.permission.READ_WIFI_CREDENTIAL"
           2403      android:protectionLevel="signature|privileged" />

     Once a permission carries the privileged flag, the allowlist check becomes an AND
     gate placed IN FRONT of the signature grant, so holding the platform key is not
     enough:

         AppIdPermissionPolicy.kt
           1143  val mayGrantByPrivileged =
           1144      !permission.isPrivileged ||
           1145          requestingPackageStates.anyIndexed { _, it ->
           1146              checkPrivilegedPermissionAllowlistIfNeeded(it, permission)
           1147          }
           ...
           1157  if (
           1158      mayGrantByPrivileged &&
           1159          (shouldGrantBySignature || shouldGrantByProtectionFlags)

     and with ro.control_privapp_permissions=enforce (vendor/build.prop) a package that
     is system AND privileged and is not listed here makes that helper return false
     (:1613), which lands the package in privilegedPermissionAllowlistViolations and
     makes onSystemReady() throw:

           1922  if (!privilegedPermissionAllowlistViolations.isEmpty()) {
           1923      throw IllegalStateException(

     That is a system_server crash at every boot. AOSP documents the consequence
     plainly: "In Android 9 and higher, privileged permissions must be allowlisted or
     the device can't boot."
     https://source.android.com/docs/core/permissions/perms-allowlist

     The counter-example that settles it is in this same image: com.android.systemui is
     built with certificate: "platform" (frameworks/base/packages/SystemUI/Android.bp)
     and STILL carries an allowlist entry for this exact permission, in
     system_ext/etc/permissions/com.android.systemui.xml. Platform signing does not
     exempt a privileged app from the privileged allowlist.

     NETWORK_SETTINGS IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT. It is signature only
     (AndroidManifest.xml:2489-2490), so it is granted by the platform key and needs no
     entry. Listing a non-privileged permission here is not harmless: it is what
     CtsPrivappPermissionsTest reports as an error.

     HOW THIS FILE IS INSTALLED. Android.bp sets privapp_allowlist, and soong installs
     it with android.PathForModuleInstall(ctx, "etc", "permissions") using
     installApkName + ".xml" (build/soong/java/app.go:1230-1234). Because the module is
     system_ext_specific, that resolves to
     /system_ext/etc/permissions/DomaWifiRelay.xml. Note that the file name is the
     MODULE name, not the package name. SystemConfig reads every xml in the directory,
     so only the package attribute below has to match.

     NOTE for whoever edits this file: an XML comment may not contain two
     consecutive hyphens, and a comment that does fails the build.
-->
<permissions>
    <privapp-permissions package="com.android.xt.domawifirelay">
        <permission name="android.permission.READ_WIFI_CREDENTIAL"/>
    </privapp-permissions>
</permissions>
